cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use or discuss this research framework, please cite the
  version of the repository you consulted. Cite a version-specific
  DOI when one becomes available.
type: generic
title: 'Intelligence Spillover, Generalization, Fluidity, Transfer, and Relay (ISGFTR)'
authors:
  - family-names: Tan
    given-names: Sizhe
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  ISGFTR is an open, theory-first research framework investigating
  intelligence spillover, generalization, fluidity, transfer, and relay.
  It proposes distinctions among generative, observed, reachable, and
  evolvable capability boundaries; structural folding and reuse;
  weak-evidence capability prospecting; selective permeability;
  system-centric multi-level learning; and evidence-bearing recursive
  relay. The repository includes conceptual studies, proposed contracts,
  illustrative cases, falsifiable hypotheses, and a validation roadmap.
  It does not claim completed empirical validation or achieved AGI.
keywords:
  - structural intelligence
  - intelligence spillover
  - generalization
  - intelligence fluidity
  - transfer learning
  - structural relay
  - capability prospecting
  - collective learning
  - system-centric intelligence
  - artificial general intelligence research
